":2007.4657534246576,"to_t":2017.5506849315068,"title":"O le Ao o le Malo","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tufuga Efi"},{"qid":"Q683","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q188477","value_label":"Flag of Samoa.svg","from_t":1949.1479452054793,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Samoa","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Samoa"}],"people":{"Q32014514":{"label":"Va'aletoa Sualauvi II","description":"O le Ao o le Malo of Samoa since 2017","enwiki":"Tuimalealiʻifano Vaʻaletoʻa Sualauvi II","summary":"Afioga Tuimalealiʻifano Vaʻaletoʻa Eti Sualauvi II (born 29 April 1947) is a Samoan politician who is the current O le Ao o le Malo (head of state) of Samoa, in office since 2017.","image":"Va'aleto'a Sualauvi II 2026 (cropped).jpg","birth":1947.323287671233,"death":null},"Q57723":{"label":"Tuilaʻepa Saʻilele Malielegaoi","description":"Prime Minister of Samoa from 1998 to 2021","enwiki":"Tuilaʻepa Saʻilele Malielegaoi","summary":"Susuga Tuilaʻepa Lupesoliai Neioti Aiono Saʻilele Malielegaoi (born 14 February 1944) is a Samoan politician and economist who is the current Leader of the Opposition of Samoa. A leader of the Human Rights Protection Party (HRPP), he served as the sixth prime minister of Samoa from 1998 to 2021.\nTuilaʻepa first entered parliament in 1981 when he won a by-election to represent the electorate of Lepā, and was subsequently appointed deputy prime minister and minister of finance in the government of Prime Minister Tofilau Eti Alesana. He also held the portfolios of Tourism and Trade, Commerce & Industry.","image":"Tuilaepa Aiono Sailele Malielegaoi 2014 (cropped).jpg","birth":1945.282191780822,"death":null},"Q5446290":{"label":"Fiamē Naomi Mataʻafa","description":"Prime Minister of Samoa from 2021 to 2025","enwiki":"Fiamē Naomi Mataʻafa","summary":"Afioga Fiamē Naomi Mataʻafa (pronounced [afɪoŋa fɪameː naomɪ mataʔafa]; born 29 April 1957) is a Samoan politician and High Chief (matai) who served as the seventh Prime Minister of Samoa from 2021 to 2025. She has led the Samoa Uniting Party (SUP) since 2025.\nThe daughter of Samoa's first prime minister Fiamē Mataʻafa Faumuina Mulinuʻu II, Mataʻafa is the first woman to serve as Samoa's head of government. A member of the Human Rights Protection Party (HRPP) until 2020, she was the first woman appointed to Cabinet in Samoa's history.","image":"Fiamē Naomi Mataʻafa in 2024 (cropped).jpg","birth":1957.323287671233,"death":null},"Q317378":{"label":"Malietoa Tanumafili II","description":"Malietoa in Samoa (1913-2007)","enwiki":"Malietoa Tanumafili II","summary":"Malietoa Tanumafili II  (4 January 1913 – 11 May 2007) was O le Ao o le Malo (head of state) of Samoa from its independence in 1962 until his death in 2007. He was bestowed with the Malietoa title in 1940 and had previously worked for the New Zealand administration as a civil servant and parliamentarian. As head of state, he initially served jointly with Tupua Tamasese Meaʻole, who died in April 1963.","image":"Malietoa Tanumafili II (cropped).jpg","birth":1913.0082191780823,"death":2007.3561643835617},"Q57523":{"label":"Tufuga Efi","description":"O le Ao o le Malo of Samoa from 2007 to 2017","enwiki":"Tui Ātua Tupua Tamasese Efi","summary":"Tui Ātua Tupua Tamasese Tupuola Tufuga Efi (born 1 March 1938) is a Samoan paramount chief, politician and statesman who served as prime minister of Samoa from 1976 to 1982, and as O le Ao o le Malo (head of state) of Samoa from 2007 to 2017. He is currently a member of the Council of Deputies, having previously sat on the council from 2004 to 2007.\nAs a paramount chief (tamaʻāiga) and head of the Tupua Tamasese lineage, he heads one of Samoa's two royal families, the Sā Tupua (descendants of Queen Salamasina); he also holds the ancient pāpā title of Tui Ātua (sovereign of Atua).","image":"Tupua Tamasese Tupuola Tufuga Efi 00 (cropped).jpg","birth":1938.1616438356164,"death":null}},"media":{"Flag of Samoa.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Flag_of_Samoa.svg/330px-Flag_of_Samoa.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Samoa.svg","author":"Original: Malietoa Tanumafili II and Tupua Tamasese Meaʻole Vector:  See the file history below for details.","license":"Public domain"},"Public Seal of Samoa.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Public_Seal_of_Samoa.svg/330px-Public_Seal_of_Samoa.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Public_Seal_of_Samoa.svg","author":"Simitukidia","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"Va'aleto'a Sualauvi II 2026 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Va%27aleto%27a_Sualauvi_II_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Va%27aleto%27a_Sualauvi_II_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Va%27aleto%27a_Sualauvi_II_2026_(cropped).jpg","author":"Government House, Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet","license":"CC0"},"Tuilaepa Aiono Sailele Malielegaoi 2014 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Tuilaepa_Aiono_Sailele_Malielegaoi_2014_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Tuilaepa_Aiono_Sailele_Malielegaoi_2014_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tuilaepa_Aiono_Sailele_Malielegaoi_2014_(cropped).jpg","author":"DFAT","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"Fiamē Naomi Mataʻafa in 2024 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Fiam%C4%93_Naomi_Mata%CA%BBafa_in_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Fiam%C4%93_Naomi_Mata%CA%BBafa_in_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fiam%C4%93_Naomi_Mata%CA%BBafa_in_2024_(cropped).jpg","author":"Number 10","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"Malietoa Tanumafili II (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Malietoa_Tanumafili_II_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Malietoa_Tanumafili_II_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malietoa_Tanumafili_II_(cropped).jpg","author":"Archives New Zealand","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"Tupua Tamasese Tupuola Tufuga Efi 00 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Tupua_Tamasese_Tupuola_Tufuga_Efi_00_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Tupua_Tamasese_Tupuola_Tufuga_Efi_00_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tupua_Tamasese_Tupuola_Tufuga_Efi_00_(cropped).jpg","author":"CloudSurfer","license":"CC BY 2.5"}},"names":["Estado Independiente de Samoa","Independent State of Samoa","Onafhankelijke Staat Samoa","SAM","Samoa","Samoa Occidentali","Samoa Zachodnie","Samoa occidentales","Unabhängiger Staat Samoa","WS","WSM","West-Samoa","Western Samoa","Westsamoa","ws","État indépendant des Samoa","Σαμόα","Независимое Государство Самоа","Самоа","ساموآ","ساموا","ساموا الغربية","समोआ","サモア","サモア独立国","萨摩亚","萨摩亚独立国","薩摩亞"]}